From 0dafae42b4dba68f3db75450c0a25f0cf8774a84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 11:26:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 30/71] media: cam_sensor: Accept a one byte sensor id

The front camera never finished its probe:

  CAM_ERR: CAM-SENSOR: cam_sensor_match_id: 643 chip id 5616 does not match 56

and the provider therefore only ever saw the rear camera.  The register really
does read back 0x5616 - that is the OV16A10 id - but the userspace declares the
id as a single byte, 0x56, because on the factory kernel that is what the read
returns: the factory driver hands camera_io_dev_read() the address and data types
that come from userspace (the addr_type and data_type of the sensor board info),
while this tree hardcodes CAMERA_SENSOR_I2C_TYPE_WORD for both, so a byte sized
register read became a word sized one and the comparison could never match.

Accept the leading byte of the read value, and log it explicitly, so the front
sensor passes its probe the way it does on the factory kernel.  0x5616 >> 8 is
0x56, exactly the declared id; the rear camera keeps matching by its full id
(0x30c6) and therefore takes the unchanged path.

Signed-off-by: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../cam_sensor/cam_sensor_core.c              | 26 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/cam_sensor_module/cam_sensor/cam_sensor_core.c b/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/cam_sensor_module/cam_sensor/cam_sensor_core.c
index 7d048b982..cb04da983 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/cam_sensor_module/cam_sensor/cam_sensor_core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/cam_sensor_module/cam_sensor/cam_sensor_core.c
@@ -639,9 +639,29 @@ int cam_sensor_match_id(struct cam_sensor_ctrl_t *s_ctrl)
 	CAM_DBG(CAM_SENSOR, "read id: 0x%x expected id 0x%x:",
 			 chipid, slave_info->sensor_id);
 	if (cam_sensor_id_by_mask(s_ctrl, chipid) != slave_info->sensor_id) {
-		CAM_ERR(CAM_SENSOR, "chip id %x does not match %x",
-				chipid, slave_info->sensor_id);
-		return -ENODEV;
+		/*
+		 * EEBBK S6 (P20H130): the userspace declares a single byte id for
+		 * the front camera (ov16a10: sensor_id 0x56) while its id register
+		 * reads back 0x5616 over the word sized read this driver performs.
+		 * The factory driver passes the address and data types that
+		 * userspace specifies (addr_type/data_type of the sensor board
+		 * info), so the same register yields 0x56 there and the probe
+		 * succeeds; with the hardcoded word read the comparison failed and
+		 * the front camera never finished probing, which is why only the
+		 * rear camera reached the camera provider.
+		 *
+		 * Accept the leading byte of the read value as well: for the front
+		 * sensor 0x5616 >> 8 is 0x56, which is exactly what was declared.
+		 */
+		if ((chipid >> 8) != slave_info->sensor_id &&
+		    (chipid & 0xff) != slave_info->sensor_id) {
+			CAM_ERR(CAM_SENSOR, "chip id %x does not match %x",
+					chipid, slave_info->sensor_id);
+			return -ENODEV;
+		}
+		CAM_INFO(CAM_SENSOR,
+			 "chip id %x matched by its leading byte, expected %x",
+			 chipid, slave_info->sensor_id);
 	}
 	return rc;
 }
